Can you give an example to get the size of `WindowSized`?
I can manage to get the ID of `WindowSized` but its `width()` or `height()` does not exist unless manually specified.



```rust
#[element_component]
fn App(hooks: &mut Hooks) -> Element {
    WindowSized::el(vec![])
        .on_spawned(|world, id, _data| {
            println!("WindowSized spawned");
            let w = world.get(id, width()).unwrap_or(0.);
            let h = world.get(id, height()).unwrap_or(0.);
            println!("WindowSized spawned: {} {}", w, h);
        })
        .with(background_color(), vec4(0.3, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0))
        .children(vec![ScrollArea {
            sizing: ScrollAreaSizing::FitParentWidth,
            inner: FlowColumn::el([
                Text::el("1111111111111111").header_style(),
                Text::el("2222222222222222").header_style(),
                Text::el("3333333333333333").header_style(),
                Text::el("4444444444444444").header_style(),
                Text::el("5555555555555555").header_style(),
                Text::el("6666666666666666").header_style(),
                Text::el("7777777777777777").header_style(),
                Text::el("8888888888888888").header_style(),
                Text::el("9999999999999999").header_style(),
            ]),
        }
        .el()])
}
```

The `ScrollArea` `.on_spawned` (inside the definition of `ScrollArea` ) can find its parent, but cannot get the `height` and `width`, which should be the screen size.

The `WindowSized` `.on_spawned` can print width and height properly.
